<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muniadona of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 995–1066</span> · Also known as Mayor of Castile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muniadona of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> (c. 995–1066), also called Mayor, was the daughter of Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-garcia-of-castile">Sancho García of Castile</a> and the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iii-of-navarre">Sancho III of Navarre</a>. After her brother García Sánchez, the last count, was murdered in 1029, Castile passed through her to her husband and then to their son Ferdinand, who became the first king of Castile and later king of León.</p></div>
